      both sit inside ONE method: the parameter is declared at line 64
      (`def put(blockId: BlockId)`) and the sink is at line 72, and the trace
      this arm attached confirms it - step 0 is `$blockId` at line 72 column 21,
      step 1 is the sink at line 72 column 13. The flow never crosses a method
      boundary, so INTRA-FILE INTER-PROCEDURAL taint - which is precisely and
      only what --taint-intrafile adds - has nothing to contribute. The default
      intraprocedural taint analysis already reaches it, and it does so in this
