      --optimizations=none toggles optimizations rather than taint; and the
      --pro family requires the proprietary Semgrep Pro Engine. Nothing disables
      taint. So 'taint off' in this A/B means 'intraprocedural taint' rather
      than 'no taint', and a reader must not take this arm as a
